  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef la_least_squares(X: list, y: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Least Squares Solution** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef la_least_squares(X: list, y: list) -> dict:\n    Xa, ya = np.array(X, dtype=np.float64), np.array(y, dtype=np.float64)\n    w = np.linalg.solve(np.dot(Xa.T, Xa), np.dot(Xa.T, ya))\n    return {'weights': np.round(w, 6).tolist(), 'residual_norm': round(float(np.linalg.norm(np.dot(Xa, w) - ya)), 6)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
